<section class="content-section">
    <div class="container">

            <div class="text-justify">
                My research interests lie in the modelling of the complex interactions between coherent nonlinear structures and turbulent fluctuations in turbulent fluid flows. This involves the understanding of both vortex dynamics, nonlinear wave interactions, and stochastic fluctuations. I predominantly deal with turbulent flows in two-dimensional and geophysical fluid dynamics (atmospheres and oceans), quantum fluids such as those appearing as Bose-Einstein Condensates (BECs) or superfluid helium, and fluid analogies in nonlinear optics and cosmology.<br>
                <br>
                Below is a selection of funding opportunities and current research projects that any potential PhD student or postdoctoral researcher who is interested in working under my supervision can apply for or freely discuss with me.
            </div>

    </div>
</section>

